(files fetched: Lato-Regular.ttf, Lato-Bold.ttf, Lato-Italic.ttf, Lato-BoldItalic.ttf,
plus this OFL.txt, from the `main` branch, 2026-08-26).

These files are redistributed unmodified under the SIL Open Font License,
Version 1.1. The full license text is in OFL.txt in this same directory —
see http://scripts.sil.org/OFL for the license and FAQ.

Why Lato: DEC-133 (Consultify PDF font fix, 2026-08-27). Server-side PDFs
generated with pdfkit defaulted to the built-in Helvetica (WinAnsi encoding),
which does not contain Polish diacritics (ą ę ł ń ó ś ź ż / Ą Ę Ł Ń Ó Ś Ź Ż) —
every Polish-language PDF Consultify generated rendered those characters as
garbage bytes. Lato is OFL (freely embeddable/redistributable, no per-seat
licensing risk), has full Polish (and broader Latin) glyph coverage via the
Google Fonts "Latin Plus" character set, and is already one of the 10 curated
fonts in docs/product/DELIVERABLE_FORMATTING_SPEC.md (§1, pairing #3 and the
"Clean" theme, docx/pptx/web-viewer surfaces) — so this choice is consistent
with, not additive to, the existing brand font library. It is registered here
for pdfkit specifically because pdfkit embeds font files directly into the
PDF byte stream (no reliance on the client machine having any given font
installed), which is the correct fix for a bug that has nothing to do with
which fonts a viewer's OS ships.
